
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.Axes2Rot(Forward: vector, Left: vector, Up: vector): rotation`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`rotation llAxes2Rot(vector Forward, vector Left, vector Up);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Returns a rotation that is defined by the 3 coordinate axes</p>
</p>
      <table class="param-table" id="parameters">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>vector</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>vector</span></td>
          <td>Forward / fwd</td>
          <td>Forward/Back part of rotation.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>vector</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>vector</span></td>
          <td>Left / left</td>
          <td>Left/Right part of rotation.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>vector</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>vector</span></td>
          <td>Up / up</td>
          <td>Up/Down part of rotation.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>math</li>
        <li>math_3d</li>
        <li>math_trig</li>
        <li>quaternion</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">17</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
        <span class="attr-label bg-pure">Side-Effect Free</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <p>All three vectors must be mutually orthogonal unit vectors.</p>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local function main()
    local i = vector(1.0, 0.0, 0.0)
    local j = vector(0.0, 1.0, 0.0)
    local k = vector(0.0, 0.0, 1.0)

    local rot = ll.Axes2Rot(j, -i, k)

    ll.Say(0, tostring(ll.Rot2Euler(rot) * RAD_TO_DEG))
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        vector i = < 1.0, 0.0, 0.0>;
        vector j = < 0.0, 1.0, 0.0>;
        vector k = < 0.0, 0.0, 1.0>;

        rotation rot = llAxes2Rot( j, -i, k );

        llSay(0, (string) (llRot2Euler(rot) * RAD_TO_DEG) );
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>This script displays:</p>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`Object: <-0.00000, 0.00000, 90.00000>`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>which shows that (<b>j</b>, <b>-i</b>, <b>k</b>) is obtained by rotating (<b>i</b>, <b>j</b>, <b>k</b>) 90 degrees around z direction.</p>
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <p>Technically, only the first two vectors are needed to define this rotation, which can be done by calling any of these:</p>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`llAxes2Rot(fwd, left, fwd % left);
llAxes2Rot(left % up, left, up);
llAxes2Rot(fwd, up % fwd, up);`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <h2>Deep Notes</h2>
  <h3>Tests</h3>
